REGISTRATION
1536 x 1536 transparent RGBA canvases. Ground root: (768, 1220) for every still
and frame. Source density: 440 px/m. Camera elevation 35.2643897 degrees,
azimuth 45 degrees; right-handed XZ ground, Y up. No frame-level recentering.
The proof cross marks the same root and every clip uses one fixed review crop.

IMPORTANT SCOPE
These are candidate illustrations, not a runtime integration. Original files and
hero assets have not been modified. Semantic state and clip IDs are preserved,
but changed silhouettes require collision, sorting, scale and import-bounds review.
Generated body volumes have BAKED artistic isometric perspective, lighting and
rounded shading. They are not mathematically exact 3D bodies. Moving component
landmarks and hinge/rail deformations use the declared mathematical projection.
Source registration is therefore a fixed-view 2.5D illustrated assembly, not a
rotatable model or proof of exact orthogonal body surfaces.

EDITABLE SOURCE
source/masters contains eight untouched NEW built-in imagegen atlases.
source/prompts contains the exact independent generation prompt for each atlas.
source/master_inventory.json records master SHA256, dimensions and generation mode.
No animation frame was independently generated. The same authored source components
are cropped, clipped, mapped and transformed throughout each clip. Source alpha is
preserved; no alpha thresholding or recoloring is used to hide generation artifacts.
source/build_workshop.py contains editable crops, landmarks, hinge transforms,
satchel flap unrolling, drawer rail motion and material-specific fracture geometry.
source/clipping_meshes.json records source-space masks; layers are derived source
components plus authored exposed material lips/fibers. These are raster illustrations
with editable Python/JSON construction, not pure-vector replacements for old SVGs.
Source reference_before PNGs and original manifests are comparison-only historical
art. They are included only so the proof rebuild is completely self-contained.

REBUILD FROM ANY EXTRACTED LOCATION
Python 3.10 or later is recommended. Install Pillow and NumPy, then run:
python source/build_delivery.py
For stills and before/after proof only:
python source/build_delivery.py --stills-only
Optional ffmpeg generates the MP4 when found on PATH. All sprite PNGs, GIFs,
proof sheets and manifests are generated without ffmpeg. A DejaVu font and its
redistribution license are bundled under source/fonts. No repository sibling,
absolute workspace path, original external pack, online service or API is required.
Image generation is not re-run by these commands.

DAMAGE LANGUAGE
Satchel: opened gusset seam and hanging leather. Sack: burst side seam and grain spill.
Hamper: lost rim/handle and torn reeds. Coffin: broken cross-grain lid planks.
Cabinet: splintered lower door rail. Scuttle: torn/folded sheet-metal seam.
Rollcase: torn cloth end seam and removed cap. Drawer: failed rail/tilted tray and
sheared front corner. No repeated central Z-shaped cutout is used.

COMPACT ARCHIVE
The complete compact delivery includes every original illustration master, exact
prompt, editable assembly source, source reference, runtime PNG state/frame,
manifest and proof. The layers directory is a rebuild cache; its extracted/derived
PNGs duplicate the masters and are regenerated by source/build_delivery.py. They
are omitted from the compact ZIP to keep one complete delivery below 100 MiB.
